{"availability":"available","full":"ishandeep48/CrowdSource_Issue","name":"CrowdSource_Issue","description":"CivicSewa is a full-stack web app that lets citizens report local civic issues like potholes, broken streetlights, and waste problems, track their status in real-time, and helps authorities manage and resolve them efficiently.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":2,"forks":3,"created":"2025-09-04T14:35:52Z","updated":"2026-01-05T17:21:24Z","branch":"Dev_Electron","homepage":"https://civicsewa.onrender.com/","topics":["bert","expressjs","gradio","huggingface","mongodb","mongoose","node-cron","nodejs","reactjs","tailwindcss","vite"],"demo":"https://civicsewa.onrender.com/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:25.734Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:25.734Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:25.734Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T22:34:25.734Z","stars":2,"forks":3}],"technologies":["React","Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A full-stack web application for reporting and tracking local issues, facilitating communication between the public and relevant authorities.","CivicSewa is a platform designed to bridge the gap between citizens and local authorities. It provides a user-friendly interface for reporting civic issues such as potholes, broken streetlights, and waste management problems. By crowdsourcing this information, the application aims to improve the efficiency of issue resolution and enhance community engagement."],"features":["User Authentication: Secure user registration and login system.","Issue Reporting: Users can report issues with details like location, description, and images.","Interactive Map: A map-based visualization of reported issues using the Google Maps API.","Role-Based Dashboards: Separate dashboards for users, department officials, and administrators with role-specific functionalities.","Local Reported Issues: User can see issues reported in their area and